#: e8d29a3865b446c5aef498021b305b69
msgid "QuadPlane Flight modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:6
#: 67b20b24ac9543c480043e80f10977c8
msgid "The QuadPlane code is based upon the Plane master firmware but with 6 extra modes. Most are identical to equivalent Copter modes:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:24
#: 66863f8ca1c04b9ba1072d35f0ab3b19
msgid "** not actually a flight mode, but rather a feature of QACRO and QSTABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:26
#: 6fda12c9462543bb8d94de0679e240b2
msgid "\\*\\*\\* not actually a flight mode, but a VTOL tuning feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:28
#: 583259716f2642e4b978a5cc23d9ec00
msgid "\\*\\*\\*\\* not actually a flight mode, but a VTOL tuning and model development tool"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:30
#: 718f2aad9c764f53be8190a420a5cef7
msgid "RTL mode can behave differently than a normal fixed wing RTL, depending on the setting of the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` parameter. See :ref:`Hybrid RTLs <hybrid_rtl>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:33
#: 559be57638554ab7b3d7239ded4859e4
msgid "You may need to set the ``FLTMODE*`` parameters for these extra modes as numeric values if your GCS doesn't understand these values yet."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:37
#: 1ee32eba2c1a4610907744c79eb51d5f
msgid "If you are familiar with the equivalent Copter flight modes then you should be comfortable flying a QuadPlane. The most significant difference comes during transition between fixed wing and QuadPlane flight, which is described :ref:`here <quadplane-flying>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:44
#: 680f0affd48d44319abc9f22871869c4
msgid "There is also a difference in throttle channel parameters from Copter: instead of :ref:`THR_DZ<THR_DZ>` for setting the deadzone, QuadPlane uses RCn_DZ (where n is the channel mapped to throttle input). The default for throttle channel deadzone is 60 (+/- 6%). If your QuadPlane does not hover at mid-stick (+/- 6%) in QSTABILIZE, you will need to center it using :ref:`Q_M_THST_HOVER<Q_M_THST_HOVER>` to set the throttle percentage applied at mid-stick in QSTABILIZE such that switching to QHOVER or QLOITER does not result in an altitude change. This value can be automatically learned and applied during QLOITER and QHOVER modes, by enabling :ref:`Q_M_HOVER_LEARN<Q_M_HOVER_LEARN>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:50
#: 74c7654e7a76416586f3c2b0fef6c411
msgid "Since QuadPlanes have much higher surface area than most Copters, hovering or loitering in a tail wind can be a challenge for stability. It is generally better to hover or loiter with the nose pointed into the wind, see :ref:`Weathervaning <quadplane-weathervaning>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:54
#: ae502d2776d244ac951f33ac8a8dbb5e
msgid "The landing detection logic in QLOITER mode is not as sophisticated as the landing detection logic in Copter, so if you get GPS movement while on the ground in QLOITER mode then the aircraft may try to tip over as it tries to hold position while in contact with the ground. It is suggested that you switch to QHOVER or QSTABILIZE once landed as these are unaffected by GPS movement."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:58
#: aabafdc217dd4160a31eaf484b6e08ad
msgid "Flight modes to avoid"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:60
#: 55e01b299b5e42fc8b143870b0dc83f3
msgid "The linked nature of the vertical lift and fixed wing control in quadplanes means the autopilot always needs to know what the pilot is trying to do in terms of speed and attitude. For this reason you should avoid the following flight modes in a quadplane:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:63
#: 239e4656be974b90aecac97c0b235262
msgid "ACRO"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:64
#: 01315eecea0543599e003ecab37254c2
msgid "STABILIZE"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:65
#: 16796f2e6e544d3889c54ada5a8b501b
msgid "TRAINING"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:67
#: ca92061cd1ab4350a650cec653ea22dd
msgid "these modes are problematic as the stick input from the pilot is not sufficient to tell the autopilot what attitude the aircraft wants or what climb rate is wanted, so the quadplane logic does not engage the quad motors when in these modes. These modes also make log analysis difficult. Please use FBWA mode instead of STABILIZE for manual flight."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:70
#: 0dc7de000c6e45629cfca309ae2985a6
msgid "In the future we may add ways to use the quad motors in these modes, but for now please avoid them."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane-flight-modes.rst:72
#: 00e225f10c6144ad969058653fd425c4
msgid "The other mode where the quad motors are disabled is MANUAL mode. That mode still can be useful for checking aircraft trim in fixed wing flight or for taxiing your aircraft."
msgstr ""
